(in-ns 'go.arbace.pyctypes) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// The limited C API's remainder (queue 268; doc/python/PYTHON-SURVEY.md, \"As built: 268\"): the functions of queue 262's"] [4 1 "// list of natives not provided (`.tmp/q262/missing.txt`) that the world's _testlimitedcapi reaches and pyi's objects"] [5 1 "// answer directly: dicts, sets, lists, tuples, ints, floats, complex numbers, bytes, bytearrays, the number, mapping"] [6 1 "// and sequence protocols, str's core, weak references, imports' module table, PyMem. Each follows its CPython 3.14.10"] [7 1 "// definition (Objects/dictobject.c, setobject.c, listobject.c, tupleobject.c, longobject.c, floatobject.c,"] [8 1 "// complexobject.c, bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c, abstract.c, unicodeobject.c, weakrefobject.c, Python/import.c,"] [9 1 "// Objects/obmalloc.c): the type checks and their messages, the operation through pyi's own (its type's method or"] [10 1 "// protocol, as CPython's calls the type's slot). The PSF's license (LICENSE.md)."] [24 1 "// callMeth calls o's method name with args."] [33 1 "// each calls f on each item of iter(o) until it returns an error (Iterate's)."] [41 1 "// callBuiltin calls builtins.name with args."] [50 1 "// opArgs are a native's object arguments, nil for NULL; err when one is NULL (null_error)."] [70 1 "// bigOf is o as an int (its __index__), CPython's _PyNumber_Index."] [82 1 "// asUnsigned is PyLong_AsUnsignedLong's family: o an int (no __index__), in [0, 2**bits)."] [101 1 "// asSignedBits is PyLong_AsInt32's family: o's __index__ in the signed range of bits."] [113 1 "// unsignedIndex is PyLong_AsUInt32's family: o's __index__ in [0, 2**bits)."] [130 1 "// storeInt writes the int v of size bytes at p (an output argument), when p is not NULL."] [147 2 "// ---- dicts (Objects/dictobject.c) ----"] [150 70 "// PyDict_Check: a subclass's instance too"] [188 34 "// _PyErr_SetKeyError"] [212 2 "// PyDict_GetItem and GetItemString: borrowed, errors suppressed; an error but KeyError (an unhashable key, a key that"] [213 2 "// does not decode) reported as unraisable (dictobject.c's dict_getitem, PyErr_FormatUnraisable)"] [238 21 "// _PyObject_HashFast's error, not the lookup's"] [304 2 "// PyDict_Next(d, Py_ssize_t *pos, PyObject **key, PyObject **value): borrowed references"] [349 2 "// ---- sets (Objects/setobject.c) ----"] [375 3 "// set_contains_key: the key hashed as is (set's `in` retries an unhashable set as a frozenset; PySet_Contains not)"] [401 4 "// a brand new frozenset (C holds its only reference: PyFrozenSet_New's) is filled in place"] [409 4 "// _PyErr_BadInternalCall(__FILE__, __LINE__) of Objects/setobject.c's PySet_Add (a frozenset too: pyi's are"] [410 4 "// never brand new to C)"] [437 2 "// ---- lists and tuples (Objects/listobject.c, tupleobject.c) ----"] [535 2 "// ---- ints (Objects/longobject.c) ----"] [565 2 "// PyLong_FromVoidPtr: a pointer that is an object's handle keeps the handle (a reference the process keeps), so that"] [566 2 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr gives the same object back while Python holds it (a handle C no longer references is released)"] [576 3 "// PyLong_FromString reads ASCII digits only (int() of a str takes the Unicode decimal digits, which"] [577 3 "// _PyUnicode_TransformDecimalAndSpaceToASCII gives it): a byte past 0x7f is long_from_string_base's invalid"] [578 3 "// literal, with the string decoded as UTF-8 (Objects/longobject.c)"] [589 20 "// the base the prefix gives, as long_from_string_base resolves it before the digits"] [627 2 "// longobject.c's messages, as they are"] [640 2 "// PyLong_AsVoidPtr: an int (no __index__: \"an integer is required\") as a pointer; NULL on an error"] [674 2 "// PyLong_AsInt32 (o, int32_t *out) and the family: 0, or -1 with an error"] [679 24 "// *value left as it was"] [695 2 "// ---- floats and complex numbers ----"] [701 3 "// a str or a buffer only (Objects/floatobject.c; queue 270): float() also takes numbers"] [720 3 "// a new sys.float_info (floatobject.c's PyFloat_GetInfo makes one each call)"] [730 2 "// PyComplex_RealAsDouble and ImagAsDouble: capi_tail.go (asCComplex)"] [731 2 "// ---- the number protocol (Objects/abstract.c) ----"] [761 2 "// ---- the mapping and sequence protocols ----"] [796 2 "// the string-keyed forms (Objects/abstract.c): a NULL object or key is null_error's SystemError, the key decoded as"] [797 2 "// PyUnicode_FromString decodes it (its UnicodeDecodeError propagates)"] [831 2 "// PyMapping_HasKey and the rest: PyMapping_GetOptionalItem's lookup, a KeyError alone meaning absent (an IndexError"] [832 2 "// propagates); the forms without WithError report any error as unraisable, by their own message, and give 0"] [989 2 "// ---- bytes and bytearrays (Objects/bytesobject.c, bytearrayobject.c) ----"] [997 2 "// PyBytes_Repr(o, smartquotes) (Objects/bytesobject.c): double quotes only when smartquotes and the bytes hold a"] [998 2 "// single quote and no double quote; else single quotes, a single quote escaped"] [1042 47 "// the mirror's ob_sval (queue 269)"] [1050 2 "// PyBytes_Concat and PyBytes_ConcatAndDel (Objects/bytesobject.c): *pv NULL does nothing, w NULL clears *pv (no"] [1051 2 "// error), else *pv becomes bytes_concat's new bytes of the two buffers (a bytes-like object each, a C-contiguous"] [1052 2 "// one: anything else \"can't concat W to V\"), NULL on an error"] [1121 2 "// PyByteArray_Concat (Objects/bytearrayobject.c): a new bytearray of the two buffers (PyBUF_SIMPLE: a C-contiguous"] [1122 2 "// bytes-like object each, else \"can't concat B to A\")"] [1160 2 "// ---- str's core (Objects/unicodeobject.c) ----"] [1174 2 "// ensureStr is unicodeobject.c's ensure_unicode: an argument that is no str a TypeError \"must be str, not T\""] [1186 2 "// PyUnicode_GetLength and PyUnicode_ReadChar: an object that is no str is PyErr_BadArgument's TypeError; ReadChar's"] [1187 2 "// error is (Py_UCS4)-1, the 32-bit all-ones"] [1221 56 "// a subclass's instance: a new exact str (_PyUnicode_Copy